    "body": "Review fixes on head d94707823 (main 9fb406cd6 merged in; the merge was clean, with no hand edits).\n\n1. Finding: a `STOP` block with `M0` or `M1` recorded two stops.\n   - Fix: `stop_block` (crates/gcode/src/klartext/blocks.rs) records one `ProgramStop`. It removes `M0` and `M1` from the list that it gives to `post_m`. `STOP` is an unconditional stop, so `M1` does not make it an optional stop. `M0` keeps its effect: spindle stop and coolant off.\n   - Test: `klartext_stop_with_m0_or_m1_records_one_program_stop` (crates/gcode/tests/klartext/paths.rs). Without the fix, the test fails with 4 stops: `[(ProgramStop, 4), (ProgramStop, 4), (ProgramStop, 6), (OptionalStop, 6)]`. With the fix, it records 2 stops, both `ProgramStop`.\n2. Finding: the PR body had no reason for the new top-level test binary `crates/gcode/tests/klartext`.\n   - Fix: the \"Tests\" section of the PR body now gives the one-line reason. `tests/parse/` is the suite of the RS-274 reader. Klartext is a different input language with its own entry point, so it has its own directory suite.\n\nGate results (head d94707823, Mac lane):\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-gcode --lib --test klartext --test parse` | ok (lib 0, klartext 25, parse 37) |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gcode --all-targets -- -D warnings` | ok |\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` | 4 steps, 0 failed (gcode build, lib, klartext, parse) |\n\nReady for a re-check.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
